# deploy-check-ci gate — enforcement sentinel (#1485)
#
# This committed marker governs whether the required-subset CI gate
# (`deploy.sh --check-required-subset`, the enumerated load-bearing check subset —
# today Check 38 hook-registry-index-freshness and Check 73
# bundle-metrics-gate-integrity) BLOCKS or merely REPORTS when an in-scope check
# FAILs. The runner reads this file directly, so the sentinel is load-bearing on
# its own; the thin CI workflow (deploy-check-ci.yml) additionally consumes the
# runner's exit code. One token governs ALL members: flipping it arms every check
# on the roster at once, so a new member joins at whatever posture this token
# already carries.
#
# SCOPE BOUNDARY — this token does NOT govern the whole of Check 73. Check 73's
# discrimination fixtures also run as an enumerated step in install-tests.yml,
# which carries no continue-on-error and no paths: filter, so a discrimination
# failure is a red check-run REGARDLESS of the token below. Reading `warn` here as
# "nothing about G3-14/G3-15 can block a merge" is wrong.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is the mode token:
#   warn      → report only (exit-0); an in-scope FAIL is surfaced but does not block.
#   enforce   → block on an in-scope FAIL (exit-1 propagates to the CI caller).
#
# Ships DORMANT (warn) during the calibration window, per the warn-mode-initial
# posture and the reflexive-pipeline-loop discipline (the introducing release
# `governance-ci-gates` dogfoods this gate green on its own PR before any flip).
# Flip the token below to `enforce` after a >=3-day warn-log review with zero false
# positives AND after the operator adds the `deploy-check-ci` job to
# `required_status_checks.contexts` via branch protection (the out-of-tree
# enforcement surface). That single-token edit, plus the branch-protection change,
# arms the gate. No code change is needed to graduate.
#
# (Token-flagged rather than presence-flagged so the file can ship now — the docs
#  reference it — while the gate stays non-blocking; mirrors close-completeness.enforce.)
warn
